There are always some surprising encounters.

292
00:11:01,040 --> 00:11:04,720
Like when I met you.

293
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:07,600
I'm going to eat something.

294
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:08,680
Suddenly, I feel a bit hungry.

295
00:11:09,680 --> 00:11:11,840
Feels like if I go for a late-night snack now,

296
00:11:11,840 --> 00:11:14,040
I could probably eat a lot.

297
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:16,080
See if there's anything else you want to eat.

298
00:11:16,080 --> 00:11:16,760
I'll make it for you.

299
00:11:18,280 --> 00:11:19,800
Do you want to cook some ramen?

300
00:11:20,720 --> 00:11:21,320
Sure.

301
00:11:21,320 --> 00:11:23,040
Because I want to eat something flavorful.

302
00:11:23,040 --> 00:11:24,400
Great, I want some too.

303
00:11:25,040 --> 00:11:25,920
Okay.

304
00:11:26,400 --> 00:11:27,200
About the ramen—

305
00:11:27,200 --> 00:11:29,640
Can you add two eggs or something?

306
00:11:29,640 --> 00:11:30,320
Okay.

307
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:32,400
Let me look it up.

308
00:11:33,240 --> 00:11:34,960
Are you checking how to cook noodles?

309
00:11:36,960 --> 00:11:38,120
You're such a perfectionist.

310
00:11:38,120 --> 00:11:41,080
Actually, you just need to put it in the pot.

311
00:11:41,400 --> 00:11:42,240
That won't do.

312
00:11:42,240 --> 00:11:43,520
I have to make it taste better for you.

313
00:11:45,520 --> 00:11:46,120
Alright.

314
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:47,680
Let's get started then.

315
00:11:54,600 --> 00:11:55,920
Try the soup and see if it's bland.

316
00:11:58,520 --> 00:11:59,480
Should we add more seasoning?

317
00:11:59,960 --> 00:12:01,840
I think we should add a bit more.

318
00:12:02,400 --> 00:12:03,400
It's still a bit bland, right?

319
00:12:03,920 --> 00:12:04,600
Yeah.

320
00:12:05,920 --> 00:12:07,840
I've already added all the seasoning from one packet.

321
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:08,520
Really?

322
00:12:08,520 --> 00:12:09,880
Then you don't need to add more.

323
00:12:09,880 --> 00:12:10,520
Let's leave it like this.

324
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:11,960
No need to open another packet.

325
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:12,280
It's fine.

326
00:12:12,280 --> 00:12:13,440
I'm planning to eat two packets anyway.

327
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:18,040
So this is how you cook it.

328
00:12:18,440 --> 00:12:19,720
Cooking it this way is faster, right?

329
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:22,920
He just said this is the "immortal's way" of eating it.

330
00:12:26,280 --> 00:12:28,200
Okay.

331
00:12:30,520 --> 00:12:31,240
Here, try it.

332
00:12:36,520 --> 00:12:37,960
Dinner is ready.

333
00:12:45,040 --> 00:12:45,720
Is it bland?

334
00:12:49,880 --> 00:12:50,560
No, it's not.

335
00:12:51,640 --> 00:12:52,480
It's a bit salty.

336
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:53,000
That's right.

337
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:54,840
Shall I add some more water for you?

338
00:12:54,840 --> 00:12:55,600
No need.

339
00:12:55,600 --> 00:12:57,400
I can drink water after I finish eating.

340
00:13:02,560 --> 00:13:04,040
Try this bowl and see if it's a bit lighter in flavor.

341
00:13:05,200 --> 00:13:05,880
No need.

342
00:13:05,880 --> 00:13:07,280
I shouldn't finish this bowl and then eat that one.

343
00:13:07,280 --> 00:13:07,600
I don't want it.

344
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:08,040
It's okay.

345
00:13:08,040 --> 00:13:08,440
No.

346
00:13:08,440 --> 00:13:09,560
Just leave me one bowl and that's fine.

347
00:13:09,560 --> 00:13:10,080
No.

348
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:11,720
I'm sick right now, so you should stay away from me.

349
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:15,080
Then I'll try yours.

350
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:20,720
Give me this bowl.

351
00:13:20,720 --> 00:13:21,640
Because I prefer stronger flavors.

352
00:13:21,640 --> 00:13:22,720
No, I just have a strong taste preference.

353
00:13:22,720 --> 00:13:23,880
Don't take it.

354
00:13:33,760 --> 00:13:35,080
There's still some ham here.

355
00:13:35,680 --> 00:13:37,080
Do you want some ham while we're at it?

356
00:13:37,800 --> 00:13:38,280
No, I'm good.

357
00:13:38,280 --> 00:13:40,200
I barely finished my second slice just now.

358
00:13:41,840 --> 00:13:43,200
I want to have a drink.

359
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:47,760
I think the guys here

360
00:13:47,760 --> 00:13:49,880
are really considerate.

361
00:13:56,600 --> 00:13:58,480
Just say yes or no.

362
00:13:58,480 --> 00:13:59,520
Yes, it's really good.

363
00:14:00,200 --> 00:14:01,160
It smells amazing.

364
00:14:01,560 --> 00:14:01,960
I’ve even forgotten.

365
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:03,360
When was the last time I had instant noodles?

366
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:06,280
You hardly ever eat this kind of thing.

367
00:14:06,600 --> 00:14:07,560
Then every time you get a checkup,

368
00:14:07,560 --> 00:14:09,640
you must be pretty satisfied with your results, right?

369
00:14:11,280 --> 00:14:12,120
It's not too bad.

370
00:14:15,080 --> 00:14:15,800
How come, you're so young,

371
00:14:15,800 --> 00:14:16,800
and already have things you're not satisfied with?

372
00:14:17,120 --> 00:14:17,640
No, I don't.

373
00:14:17,640 --> 00:14:19,840
You know, I just think having a regular routine

374
00:14:19,840 --> 00:14:20,560
is really important.

375
00:14:20,560 --> 00:14:21,320
In the past two years,

376
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:24,000
there were always some minor health indicators that were off.

377
00:14:24,360 --> 00:14:25,680
What did they say about you?

378
00:14:25,680 --> 00:14:26,640
Did they say your looks are too good?

379
00:14:26,640 --> 00:14:27,280
Not up to standard?

380
00:14:30,400 --> 00:14:32,120
So this year,

381
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:34,320
none of my health indicators are abnormal.

382
00:14:34,840 --> 00:14:35,680
That's good.

383
00:14:36,120 --> 00:14:39,120
I feel like just having a regular daily routine

384
00:14:39,120 --> 00:14:39,760
is all there is to it.

385
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:41,240
Eat less takeout.

386
00:14:42,680 --> 00:14:43,040
Let me tell you,

387
00:14:43,040 --> 00:14:44,640
the food at our company is amazing.

388
00:14:45,120 --> 00:14:46,960
I think your company is really great.

389
00:14:47,640 --> 00:14:48,640
Getting off work at 5:30

390
00:14:48,640 --> 00:14:51,520
is already much better than a lot of companies.

391
00:14:51,520 --> 00:14:52,280
For your industry,

392
00:14:52,280 --> 00:14:53,840
I don't think people usually get off work on time.

393
00:14:54,240 --> 00:14:55,800
It depends on what you do.

394
00:14:56,280 --> 00:14:59,040
It actually doesn't have much to do with the industry.

395
00:14:59,040 --> 00:14:59,720
You know,

396
00:15:12,040 --> 00:15:13,160
So strange.

397
00:15:13,160 --> 00:15:14,320
Really strange.

398
00:15:14,320 --> 00:15:16,480
How did it all end up after coming back from Xishuangbanna?

399
00:15:16,480 --> 00:15:18,280
At least you all have your own conversations.

400
00:15:18,280 --> 00:15:20,320
I don't even have that element of chatting.

401
00:15:20,320 --> 00:15:22,240
No one ever says they want to talk to me.

402
00:15:25,080 --> 00:15:26,560
I didn't understand the last sentence in his letter at all.

403
00:15:26,560 --> 00:15:27,560
To be honest,

404
00:15:27,960 --> 00:15:29,280
what's the biggest regret?

405
00:15:29,280 --> 00:15:30,920
How did I become the biggest regret?

406
00:15:30,920 --> 00:15:32,360
What's the regret about?

407
00:15:32,360 --> 00:15:33,160
Just talk once.

408
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:34,640
I don't want to talk to him again.

409
00:15:34,640 --> 00:15:36,440
If he wants to talk to me, I can accept it.

410
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:41,080
If you really think

411
00:15:41,080 --> 00:15:42,320
this will make you feel bad,

412
00:15:42,320 --> 00:15:43,920
then just talk openly.

413
00:15:43,920 --> 00:15:45,080
I'm not going to talk to him.

414
00:15:45,080 --> 00:15:46,600
Aren't you a bit upset?

415
00:15:46,600 --> 00:15:47,320
I'm not upset.

416
00:15:47,320 --> 00:15:48,520
I'm just confused.

417
00:15:49,280 --> 00:15:50,040
I'm confused too.

418
00:15:50,040 --> 00:15:51,360
Yeah, just confused.

419
00:15:51,640 --> 00:15:52,080
I'm not saying

420
00:15:52,080 --> 00:15:53,240
I have to get

421
00:15:53,240 --> 00:15:54,320
an answer from him.

422
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:55,640
I just feel

423
00:15:56,720 --> 00:15:58,880
your letter was unclear.

424
00:15:58,880 --> 00:16:00,440
I didn't understand it.

425
00:16:02,280 --> 00:16:04,040
Maybe you didn't want to convey

426
00:16:04,040 --> 00:16:11,040
a more definite message.

427
00:16:11,480 --> 00:16:12,480
I don't know.

428
00:16:15,920 --> 00:16:17,040
Teacher Liang

429
00:16:17,520 --> 00:16:19,760
Aren't you and Xiao Hu mutually interested?

430
00:16:19,760 --> 00:16:20,600
We are.

431
00:16:20,600 --> 00:16:22,320
But I think this person,

432
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:23,440
he hasn't figured things out yet.

433
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:24,680
He doesn't know what's going on with himself.

434
00:16:26,480 --> 00:16:28,320
He just overthinks everything.

435
00:16:29,960 --> 00:16:31,560
They're all so timid, it's unbearable.

436
00:16:34,520 --> 00:16:35,880
I think so too.

437
00:16:37,360 --> 00:16:39,240
My thought is, I just ended up with this situation.

438
00:16:39,560 --> 00:16:41,360
Just happened to get someone like this.

439
00:16:41,360 --> 00:16:42,280
Yeah.

440
00:16:43,800 --> 00:16:44,840
So what can I do?

441
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:45,280
It is what it is.

442
00:16:45,280 --> 00:16:46,360
What should I do?

443
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:49,520
I guess we just have to wait patiently.

444
00:16:55,680 --> 00:16:56,680
Since entering the cabin,

445
00:16:56,680 --> 00:16:58,800
I've been constantly thinking about many things.

446
00:16:58,800 --> 00:17:00,400
And I've been struggling internally the whole time.

447
00:17:05,920 --> 00:17:06,760
So

448
00:17:07,240 --> 00:17:09,720
I want to adjust my state properly

449
00:17:24,720 --> 00:17:25,320
Go

450
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:27,920
Hurry up

451
00:17:28,240 --> 00:17:29,280
What?

452
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:31,840
Right, left, up

453
00:17:31,840 --> 00:17:32,320
Nice

454
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:33,200
One more time, go

455
00:17:33,200 --> 00:17:33,840
Girls, heads up

456
00:17:33,840 --> 00:17:35,800
One, two, three, four

457
00:17:36,640 --> 00:17:37,200
Go

458
00:17:37,200 --> 00:17:38,680
One, two, three

459
00:17:42,360 --> 00:17:43,720
Let's go.

460
00:17:43,720 --> 00:17:44,920
Let's go eat.

461
00:17:48,480 --> 00:17:50,120
How about some Vietnamese pho?

462
00:17:50,640 --> 00:17:51,720
Sure, my treat.

463
00:17:52,160 --> 00:17:52,880
You all scan this.

464
00:17:52,880 --> 00:17:53,840
Then I'll handle that.

465
00:17:55,040 --> 00:17:58,160
It's Ms. Ka's time to return the favor.

466
00:17:58,680 --> 00:17:59,840
Wanwan, you can eat, right?

467
00:17:59,840 --> 00:18:00,440
I can eat.

468
00:18:00,440 --> 00:18:01,760
I just want to eat a lot.

469
00:18:01,760 --> 00:18:02,680
But I can't eat that much.

470
00:18:02,680 --> 00:18:03,800
Of course.

471
00:18:04,480 --> 00:18:06,600
I'm the one who cleans up the table.

472
00:18:06,600 --> 00:18:07,400
That's great.

473
00:18:07,400 --> 00:18:08,240
I'm the cleaner.

474
00:18:08,240 --> 00:18:08,840
That's great.

475
00:18:08,840 --> 00:18:09,200
Okay.

476
00:18:09,200 --> 00:18:10,040
Not just a truck.

477
00:18:10,040 --> 00:18:11,360
It's a garbage truck.

478
00:18:14,040 --> 00:18:14,920
A garbage truck.

479
00:18:14,920 --> 00:18:16,720
That's great.

480
00:18:18,760 --> 00:18:19,680
I think today you...

481
00:18:19,680 --> 00:18:21,520
Both of you guys made progress.

482
00:18:21,520 --> 00:18:22,280
Because at first, I thought...

483
00:18:22,280 --> 00:18:23,120
When you were tied up...

484
00:18:23,120 --> 00:18:24,440
You were actually a bit uncomfortable.

485
00:18:24,440 --> 00:18:26,200
Because it was unknown and kind of embarrassing.

486
00:18:26,200 --> 00:18:27,760
At that moment, I really felt like...

487
00:18:27,760 --> 00:18:29,760
a bullfrog being roasted on a grill.

488
00:18:38,680 --> 00:18:39,480
So funny.

489
00:18:40,120 --> 00:18:41,240
Look, Wanwan is still trying to cover up.

490
00:18:41,240 --> 00:18:42,840
You were really just grinning there.

491
00:18:43,200 --> 00:18:44,280
After finishing that jump just now,

492
00:18:44,280 --> 00:18:45,320
it doesn't matter anymore.

493
00:18:49,080 --> 00:18:50,040
True.

494
00:18:51,080 --> 00:18:51,760
That thing just now—

495
00:18:53,400 --> 00:18:54,160
it doesn't matter anymore.

496
00:18:57,080 --> 00:18:58,600
So when you two were in the back,

497
00:18:58,600 --> 00:19:00,160
and saw us two girls in front,

498
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:01,440
how did you feel?

499
00:19:01,440 --> 00:19:02,840
I think you danced really well.

500
00:19:03,440 --> 00:19:04,480
Thank you.

501
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:06,080
Really great.

502
00:19:06,080 --> 00:19:07,040
Yes.

503
00:19:07,040 --> 00:19:07,640
Very coordinated, really good.

504
00:19:07,640 --> 00:19:09,360
I'll just wait here for you.

505
00:19:17,520 --> 00:19:18,480
Lao Luo has gone crazy.

506
00:19:18,840 --> 00:19:20,240
No, he’s not crazy.

507
00:19:20,240 --> 00:19:21,760
He’s always been like this.

508
00:19:23,360 --> 00:19:24,520
I think that’s just how air signs are.

509
00:19:24,520 --> 00:19:25,280
“The three eccentrics.”

510
00:19:25,280 --> 00:19:26,320
When is your birthday?

511
00:19:26,760 --> 00:19:27,640
I’m a water sign.

512
00:19:27,640 --> 00:19:28,320
Cancer.

513
00:19:28,320 --> 00:19:28,840
Cancer.

514
00:19:28,840 --> 00:19:29,320
Right.

515
00:19:30,200 --> 00:19:31,400
Aren’t you always teaming up with Lao Su?

516
00:19:31,400 --> 00:19:32,360
I’m the same as Lao Su.

517
00:19:32,600 --> 00:19:33,120
Who?

518
00:19:33,560 --> 00:19:33,880
Who?

519
00:19:33,880 --> 00:19:35,440
Your old crush, the second generation.

520
00:19:35,960 --> 00:19:36,600
Don’t say that.

521
00:19:36,600 --> 00:19:37,680
If you put it that way,

522
00:19:37,680 --> 00:19:39,320
I actually have quite a few “crushes.”

523
00:19:40,520 --> 00:19:42,760
You’re the original old crush.

524
00:19:44,560 --> 00:19:47,080
Chen is the second generation old crush.

525
00:19:47,600 --> 00:19:49,880
Yonghao is the third generation old crush.

526
00:19:50,520 --> 00:19:51,440
All the dates count.

527
00:19:51,800 --> 00:19:52,880
What about Lao Hou?

528
00:19:52,880 --> 00:19:54,560
Which generation old crush is Lao Hou?

529
00:19:54,920 --> 00:19:56,160
I don’t know, you have too many.

530
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:58,200
That’s a dangerous thing to say.

531
00:19:58,200 --> 00:19:59,320
Ms. Xia.

532
00:19:59,320 --> 00:20:02,760
She’s already started scolding like crazy.

533
00:20:03,760 --> 00:20:04,560
That’s good.

534
00:20:04,560 --> 00:20:06,120
You just need to interact with everyone more.

535
00:20:06,120 --> 00:20:07,520
You might get a better idea

536
00:20:07,520 --> 00:20:09,120
of what you really want.

537
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:14,440
I think what I want is

538
00:20:14,960 --> 00:20:16,160
a relaxed life,

539
00:20:16,720 --> 00:20:17,920
and an easygoing partner.

540
00:20:19,480 --> 00:20:20,600
What counts as easygoing?

541
00:20:21,440 --> 00:20:23,320
Not having too many arguments or disagreements.

542
00:20:23,600 --> 00:20:25,360
But those are bound to happen in life.

543
00:20:25,360 --> 00:20:25,760
They will happen.

544
00:20:25,760 --> 00:20:27,000
But I don't want too many of them.

545
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:27,840
Because I've been through that before.

546
00:20:27,840 --> 00:20:29,040
A lot of arguments and disagreements.

547
00:20:29,040 --> 00:20:29,920
It made me feel exhausted.

548
00:20:31,520 --> 00:20:32,920
You know I really enjoy

549
00:20:34,080 --> 00:20:35,320
even after getting a boyfriend,

550
00:20:35,320 --> 00:20:36,360
hanging out with my boyfriend's friends

551
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:37,200
and my girlfriends too.

552
00:20:37,200 --> 00:20:38,680
I like everyone having fun together.

553
00:20:38,680 --> 00:20:39,520
But

554
00:20:39,520 --> 00:20:40,800
maybe like Lao Luo said,

555
00:20:40,800 --> 00:20:41,880
a lot of people who like me

556
00:20:41,880 --> 00:20:42,960
might be more introverted.

557
00:20:42,960 --> 00:20:43,840
They might feel

558
00:20:43,840 --> 00:20:45,080
that they need someone as lively as me.

559
00:20:45,080 --> 00:20:45,640
Yes.

560
00:20:45,640 --> 00:20:46,600
And then he might think

561
00:20:46,600 --> 00:20:48,040
that a relationship should just be between two people,

562
00:20:48,040 --> 00:20:48,720
or something like that.

563
00:20:48,720 --> 00:20:49,600
But I feel

564
00:20:49,600 --> 00:20:51,120
I also need time for just the two of us,

565
00:20:51,120 --> 00:20:52,560
of course I really need that,

566
00:20:52,560 --> 00:20:54,840
but I also need to have fun with everyone together.

567
00:20:54,840 --> 00:20:57,160
And then gradually, with all sorts of things,

568
00:20:57,160 --> 00:20:57,960
differences start to appear.

569
00:20:57,960 --> 00:20:58,720
Right.

570
00:20:58,720 --> 00:20:59,360
When two people are together,

571
00:20:59,360 --> 00:21:00,280
it's actually like this.

572
00:21:00,640 --> 00:21:02,040
He has to keep exploring,

573
00:21:02,040 --> 00:21:03,160
all your different sides.

574
00:21:03,160 --> 00:21:04,480
And among all those sides,

575
00:21:04,480 --> 00:21:06,000
